# Who can put what in MAIL FROM, for [% domain %].
#
# smtpd_sender_login_maps.  reject_authenticated_sender_login_mismatch in
# smtpd_sender_restrictions enforces it.  postfix rejects an authenticated
# client if its SASL login name does not own the MAIL FROM address.  It also
# rejects an address that is not here, because nobody owns it.  So the recipe
# makes this file from the accounts and the aliases together.
#
# The login name is the full address, because the dovecot passwd file uses it
# as its key.
#
# This table does not apply to unauthenticated senders.  DMARC deals with them.
[% FOR login IN sender_logins %]
[% login.address %] [% login.owner %]
[%- END %]
